  "run_status": "ok",
  "summary": "The paper is mostly arithmetically coherent. The pilot funnel (70 hits, 36 duplicates, 34 unique), the 5/8/21 coding split, Tables 3 and 4 (33/34 = 97%), the 3,187/92/43 counts, Table 6 (19+10 = 29 and 19+10+9+5 = 43), the 18/17/26/2 ceremony counts and Table 8 (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579, with every share rounding correctly) all reproduce. I found five material issues. (1) The \"2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)\" yield statistic uses distinct openings as the numerator and articles as the denominator. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 and Section 4.1 show the second coder coded it relevant. (3) Section 6.2 says \"between a third and a half\", but two Table 7 shares are 52% and 55%. (4) The text says only Q1 2024 is missing, but the stated data gap runs January to April 2024. (5) The word-classification precedence rule in Appendix A.3.2 conflicts with its own bysykkelstativ example, and its effect on Table 8 cannot be quantified. The structured table CSVs were not used. Values were read from the page text and page images, as the parser-quality guidance recommends.",
