      "claim_text": "Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.",
      "assessment": "partially",
      "cannot_verify_reason": null,
      "evidence_summary": "2/34 = 5.9%, so the arithmetic is right. But '2' is the number of distinct openings (Homborsund and Stod/Steinkjer), as Figure 1 ('Distinct openings that took place 2') and Section 3.1.4 ('Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found') show. Section 3.1.4 and Table 2 count 5 relevant articles for those two openings (4 for Homborsund, 1 for Stod). Two of the Homborsund articles predate the opening, leaving 3 post-opening articles. Figure 1 itself reports 5 relevant articles, '15 % retained'. The sentence therefore mixes an events numerator with an articles denominator. The caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits' has the same mismatch. The abstract's wording, 'two actual openings', is fine.",
