        "comparability": "All four quantities refer to the same 34-article pilot sample. They count different units: articles (5, or 3 after excluding pre-opening articles) versus distinct openings (2). A 6% article-level share is therefore not supported by the paper's own article counts.",
        "observed_discrepancy": "An events-to-articles ratio (2/34 = 5.9%) is presented as the share of articles that concern an opening. The paper's article-level counts give 5/34 = 14.7% (Figure 1, 15%) or 3/34 = 8.8% (post-opening only).",
        "possible_explanation": "The authors may have meant that the 34 articles yield only 2 distinct openings, not that 2 articles concern an opening.",
        "suggested_correction": "Rephrase as '34 unique articles yield only 2 distinct openings' and give the article-level yield separately (5 relevant, or 3 after excluding pre-opening articles). Apply the same fix to the Figure 1 caption's 'Only 2 of 70 search hits'."
