      "id": "NUM-005",
      "category": "classification_rule_vs_example",
      "finding_summary": "Appendix A.3.2 says a word fitting several types gets the first type in Table 9, but its bysykkelstativ example (and Figure 2's colouring of syklende) follows a different precedence. The effect on Table 8 and Figure 2 shares cannot be quantified.",
      "issue_type": "cannot_verify",
      "severity": "low",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "location": {
        "page": 18,
        "page_label": "18",
        "section": "A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions",
        "text_quote": "it is given the first type in the table",
        "precision": "exact"
      },
      "claim_text": "If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing 'bysykkel' (city bike), such as 'bysykkelstativ', are counted as infrastructure.",
      "assessment": "cannot_verify",
      "cannot_verify_reason": "The word-level classification output and the order in which the rules were applied are not retained. The size of the effect on the Table 8 type shares cannot be computed from the manuscript.",
      "evidence_summary": "Table 9 lists the types in the order: the word 'bicycle', Proximity, Parking & storage, Leisure, Infrastructure, Other. 'bysykkelstativ' contains 'stativ' (Parking & storage) and 'bysykkel' (Infrastructure). Under 'first type in the table' it would be Parking & storage, but the text and Figure 2 (blue bar) classify it as infrastructure. 'syklende' is listed under Infrastructure but contains 'sykle', a Proximity term, and is also shown as infrastructure in Figure 2. So the stated precedence rule and the reported classification disagree for at least these two words. They account for 0.5% and 0.3% of listings in Figure 2. Table 8 and Figure 2 report shares for these types (Infrastructure 13.4%, Parking & storage 10.8%, Proximity 10.7%). Overlap with other words in the same listings is not given.",
